::U6F5_01::A protective factor {=reduces risk or supports healthy action ~guarantees no difficulty ~is peer pressure ~proves diagnosis}

::U6F5_02::Assertive refusal includes {=clear no, reason/value, alternative, exit, and support ~a vague maybe ~a long debate ~personal disclosure}

::U6F5_03::An impaired-ride plan should {=refuse and activate safe transport backup ~depend on a promise ~wait in the car ~hide concern}

::U6F5_04::Information for responders includes {=location, observed signs, and known substances ~only a name ~a rumor ~no details}

::U6F5_05::A recovery position is used {=when appropriate while monitoring and awaiting help ~instead of calling ~to force vomiting ~to end observation}

::U6F5_06::An immediate life threat requires {=emergency services ~an influencer ~a seller ~a homework forum}

::U6F5_07::A credible ongoing-care resource is {=a licensed medical or behavioral-health professional ~an anonymous account ~an advertisement ~a rumor}

::U6F5_08::A complete action plan includes {=trigger, action, first resource, backup, barrier solution, and goal link ~only a goal ~only a number ~only refusal}
